              "help": {
                "markdown": "\n## Details\n\nAngularJS escapes interpolated values by default condidering values to be untrusted. This means that values rendered are sanitized against attacks like Cross-site Scripting (XSS) making the application more secure by deafult. Disabling Strict Contextual escaping (SCE) disables this protection and provide an additional attack surface.\n\n## Best practices for prevention\n* Avoid disabling Strict Contextual escaping (SCE)\n\n\n## References\n* [Angular $sce](https://docs.angularjs.org/api/ng/service/$sce#can-i-disable-sce-completely-)",
